# Google Drive integration — copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored. Never commit a real client secret.
#
# The credentials below belong to the "Web application" OAuth client of the
# Google Cloud project that hosts the Drive API. The same values are read at
# runtime through `import.meta.env.*` and typed in `src/vite-env.d.ts`.

# Public client id. Not a secret: it is visible in any request the app makes to
# Google. Google requires the value to end in `.apps.googleusercontent.com`.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=680907460847-antlg766lcndvtrjmhesf3jm1evjhvpl.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Client secret of the same OAuth client.
#
# THIS VALUE IS BUNDLED INTO THE SHIPPED JAVASCRIPT. That is a conscious product
# decision, not an oversight: the authorization code + PKCE exchange requires
# `client_secret` (Google answers `400 invalid_request` /
# "client_secret is missing." without it) and this project has no backend to
# hold it. Google does not treat this value as a real secret for "Web
# application" clients — the practical risk is phishing/impersonation of the app
# identity, not data exfiltration, because a holder of the secret can only mint
# tokens for their own account. The real mitigations are the scope
# (`drive.file`, non-sensitive) and the restrictions configured in Google Cloud.
#
# When the app is no longer in spike, rotate this value and, if a backend is ever
# introduced, move the exchange server-side and drop it from the bundle.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-me.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Redirect uri registered as an authorized redirect uri for the client above.
# The redirect lands in a browser tab that then hands the code back to the main
# window, so it must be a page the SPA serves (not a non-existent path).
# Production: https://juandavid.site/
VITE_GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/